        "title": "3D Reconstruction and SLAM",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Two views give one 3D point (guide 06). *Many* views, jointly, give a whole scene *and*\nthe camera trajectory that produced them. That joint recovery has two names depending on\ncontext: **Structure-from-Motion** (SfM) when done offline from a photo collection, and\n**SLAM** (Simultaneous Localization And Mapping) when done online on a moving robot or\nphone. Both solve the same problem — estimate camera poses and 3D structure together — and\nboth are refined by the same optimizer: **bundle adjustment**."
    }
